WEBVTT

00:12.410 --> 00:13.990
40-15

00:38.640 --> 00:41.770
Game, set and match, Yahiro.

00:41.770 --> 00:43.440
Two sets to love.

00:52.530 --> 00:54.450
Good game, Ran-senpai.

00:54.450 --> 00:56.160
Use this towel, please.

00:56.160 --> 00:57.330
Use my towel, please.

00:57.330 --> 00:58.790
All right, I know!

00:58.790 --> 01:00.710
First, form a queue.

01:00.710 --> 01:02.000
We'll go in the "A, I, U, E, O" order.

01:03.960 --> 01:05.670
Come on, queue up.

01:11.760 --> 01:13.600
The true forms

01:13.340 --> 01:13.600
Of the things that I gazed at

01:15.220 --> 01:15.470
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

01:16.310 --> 01:19.180
Shigofumi

01:18.930 --> 01:19.180
Again today, time

01:20.770 --> 01:21.020
Will only construct a loneliness

01:22.600 --> 01:22.850
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:29.990 --> 01:30.240
There are people who can't forget about

01:33.660 --> 01:33.910
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:37.290 --> 01:37.540
Nevertheless, recollections

01:41.080 --> 01:41.290
Visit from the future

01:44.710 --> 01:44.960
Words that turn into sighs

01:52.130 --> 01:52.380
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:55.800 --> 01:56.050
Will I flutter apart?

01:59.520 --> 01:59.770
Growing confused and disordered

02:03.230 --> 02:03.480
I want to carve

02:05.520 --> 02:05.770
These letters to you

02:10.530 --> 02:10.780
Pieces of the truth

02:12.360 --> 02:12.610
Of things that I want to tell you-

02:14.240 --> 02:14.490
I can't even send them well to you

02:17.990 --> 02:18.240
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:21.660 --> 02:21.910
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:25.330 --> 02:25.580
Even if the one word left behind

02:28.840 --> 02:31.550
To us who live

02:31.300 --> 02:31.550
Is to be goodbye

02:38.220 --> 02:41.140
News on the training camp

02:41.810 --> 02:44.310
What do you think of the freshmen this year?

02:44.310 --> 02:46.480
I guess it's great that they're so full of energy.

02:47.270 --> 02:52.070
But Nanae, you have to stop them. It happens every time.

02:52.070 --> 02:53.400
What for?

02:53.400 --> 02:56.280
The juniors are just hanging around their wonderful senior.

02:56.280 --> 02:58.200
Cold-hearted woman!

02:58.740 --> 03:01.410
Then, I'll teach you a way to deal with them.

03:01.410 --> 03:03.120
Sounds good.

03:04.910 --> 03:06.460
Get a boyfriend.

03:09.000 --> 03:11.250
Stop teasing me, Nanae.

03:12.590 --> 03:15.550
You want to be teased anyway.

03:20.850 --> 03:23.560
You really are a tease.

03:35.150 --> 03:37.610
Yahiro Kouji

03:35.150 --> 03:37.610
and Ran

03:35.150 --> 03:37.610
So, she and her father live alone together?

03:37.610 --> 03:39.870
Isn't the house a little large for them?

03:39.870 --> 03:41.330
We shouldn't pry.

03:41.330 --> 03:44.410
Aren't you curious about the thickness?

03:44.700 --> 03:46.660
You know why, right Fumika?

03:46.660 --> 03:49.460
There's so much inside. I wonder what was written.

03:49.460 --> 03:51.340
I can't tell you, obviously.

03:51.340 --> 03:55.380
Don't be stingy! You're always so secretive.

03:55.380 --> 03:58.380
It's a rule set by the Gospel Department, not me.

03:58.680 --> 04:00.720
Then, what about that guy from before?

04:01.800 --> 04:04.680
The guy wearing glasses who followed you up to the rooftop.

04:04.680 --> 04:07.390
You knew him when you were still human, right?

04:19.030 --> 04:20.870
Mikawa, why did you...

04:21.700 --> 04:24.040
Why did you shoot your father?

04:24.330 --> 04:25.450
Ehh?!

04:25.450 --> 04:27.250
There must be some reason, right?

04:27.830 --> 04:30.420
I've been looking for you, ever since then.

04:32.040 --> 04:33.670
0913.

04:33.670 --> 04:35.420
Uh, but...

04:37.920 --> 04:39.590
0913.

04:39.880 --> 04:41.050
Okay then.

04:48.600 --> 04:50.770
Mika... Mikawa!

04:51.400 --> 04:54.230
So, so, who is he?

04:54.940 --> 04:57.190
He sounded quite frantic.

04:57.490 --> 04:59.610
Could he be your boyfriend?

04:59.610 --> 05:00.740
I don't know.

05:00.740 --> 05:02.280
Ehhh?

05:02.280 --> 05:05.030
Aren't we certified partners?

05:05.030 --> 05:08.790
Partners have to have a trusting relationship, right?

05:08.790 --> 05:10.000
I'm going.

05:15.590 --> 05:17.300
You've got mail!

05:17.630 --> 05:19.300
You're a postman?

05:19.300 --> 05:22.510
Not quite, since this is a Shigofumi.

05:22.510 --> 05:23.890
Shigo...?

05:24.180 --> 05:26.640
It's a letter from the world of the departed.

05:26.640 --> 05:28.600
That's why it's called a Shigofumi.

05:29.140 --> 05:31.560
World of the departed?

05:32.140 --> 05:35.570
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry. Maybe next time.

05:36.190 --> 05:37.570
Tateishi Naoko.

05:42.280 --> 05:44.490
That's the sender's name.

05:48.950 --> 05:50.660
I don't know who that is.

05:54.460 --> 05:57.340
Well, I guess that's a normal reaction.

05:57.340 --> 06:00.260
But, what was that? It sure gets on my nerves.

06:00.260 --> 06:04.050
I'm not going to deliver your letters when you die!

06:04.340 --> 06:06.300
Kamome Station

06:09.560 --> 06:10.270
Asa!

06:10.270 --> 06:10.980
Here!

06:10.980 --> 06:13.020
Thank you. Here's one for you.

06:13.020 --> 06:14.600
Who wants this one?

06:28.200 --> 06:29.540
Why now?

06:32.960 --> 06:34.420
You had such a scary look.

06:34.420 --> 06:35.750
Did something happen?

06:36.210 --> 06:37.630
No.

06:37.630 --> 06:38.340
Really?

06:38.340 --> 06:41.550
Captain, Ran-senpai, would you like to join us?

06:41.550 --> 06:42.670
Let's play Old Maid?

06:42.970 --> 06:46.550
Would you girls cut it out? Be considerate to the other passengers.

06:47.140 --> 06:49.350
Come on. It's okay, right, Captain?

06:49.350 --> 06:52.930
That's our Ran-senpai, so understanding.

06:52.930 --> 06:56.400
In exchange, those who lose will have
to do ten sets of sprints around the court.

06:56.400 --> 06:58.770
Ehhh?

06:58.770 --> 07:00.020
Just kidding.

07:00.480 --> 07:02.650
That was mean, Senpai.

07:12.950 --> 07:16.370
What are we going to do, Fumika? They've left Kamome City.

07:16.370 --> 07:18.500
Then, we have no choice but to request an outfield trip.

07:18.500 --> 07:21.500
Yay! It's been a while since we had one!

07:21.500 --> 07:23.460
We can get out of here.

07:23.760 --> 07:26.090
Do you dislike this town, Kanaka?

07:26.090 --> 07:31.430
I love it here. But, if you eat your favorite dish
everyday, you'll get sick of it eventually, right?

07:31.890 --> 07:33.390
You can't even eat.

07:33.390 --> 07:34.680
Whatever!

07:36.440 --> 07:39.940
Dear, don't you have to hurry?

07:41.190 --> 07:45.240
Well, in this world, it's best when a police detective isn't busy.

07:45.240 --> 07:46.650
Honestly.

07:46.950 --> 07:47.950
Father.

07:48.530 --> 07:51.200
I saw Mikawa on the day of that incident.

07:55.370 --> 07:58.370
Mikawa Fumika?

07:58.670 --> 08:00.420
That's right. What's the matter?

08:02.170 --> 08:03.210
Father?

08:04.170 --> 08:06.380
That's... impossible!

08:14.180 --> 08:16.180
Sumire Garden

08:18.140 --> 08:18.190
Tennis Courts

08:18.190 --> 08:18.230
Sumire Garden

08:34.790 --> 08:38.250
Oh, so you're captain this year, Nanae-chan?

08:38.250 --> 08:40.580
Yes. Pleasure to work with you.

08:40.580 --> 08:42.000
Likewise.

08:42.290 --> 08:45.000
The order is written here.

08:47.260 --> 08:49.510
I'll be able to deliver them around 5 o'clock. Will that be all right?

08:49.510 --> 08:50.680
Yes.

08:50.680 --> 08:54.350
I'll need to check the storehouse for these. Give me a moment.

08:58.730 --> 08:59.440
Welcome.

08:59.890 --> 09:02.270
Okay, let's buy a bunch of stuff.

09:03.150 --> 09:05.270
Why are you making those sleazy noises?

09:06.320 --> 09:07.570
Just wait a bit more, okay?

09:07.570 --> 09:09.030
S-Sure.

09:14.160 --> 09:17.790
Do you think women that go out with guys are filthy?

09:18.540 --> 09:21.460
You really dislike men, don't you, Ran?

09:21.460 --> 09:23.250
I'm living with my father.

09:23.250 --> 09:25.380
You can't consider him a guy.

09:30.510 --> 09:32.510
Aren't you going a bit far for a prank?

09:32.510 --> 09:34.140
This isn't a prank.

09:35.220 --> 09:38.390
The sender is Tateishi Naoko.

09:38.390 --> 09:39.730
Tateishi?

09:40.350 --> 09:43.060
Weren't <i>you</i> the one who abandoned me?

09:44.480 --> 09:46.690
I don't think I have a reason to accept it.

09:47.270 --> 09:49.320
There's a reason for it to get delivered though.

09:50.150 --> 09:51.200
Because it's your job?

09:52.070 --> 09:53.110
Correct.

09:53.610 --> 09:55.740
Either way, I'm not accepting it.

09:57.990 --> 10:00.290
Looks like she doesn't like you very much.

10:00.290 --> 10:01.710
It's not uncommon.

10:02.000 --> 10:03.580
That's true.

10:03.580 --> 10:07.170
Receiving letters from dead people
would be called "Horror", wouldn't it?

10:07.710 --> 10:08.840
It'll be fine.

10:08.840 --> 10:09.460
Huh?

10:10.050 --> 10:12.380
This Shigofumi <i>will</i> be delivered.

10:12.380 --> 10:15.430
Ohh, young folks sure are optimistic.

10:15.970 --> 10:17.560
It's Chiaki. Why are you here?

10:18.100 --> 10:19.970
On an outfield trip all the way out here?

10:19.970 --> 10:21.930
You sure are hardworking.

10:25.440 --> 10:26.520
0923.

10:30.780 --> 10:32.150
It's been a while.

10:32.490 --> 10:34.780
We had just met recently up there.

10:34.780 --> 10:37.370
Ah, I forgot! That's right.

10:37.370 --> 10:39.200
This is Chiaki's delivery zone.

10:39.950 --> 10:43.210
It's the partner's job to determine the delivery zone.

10:43.210 --> 10:45.370
It's human nature to forget.

10:46.750 --> 10:48.500
Shut up, Tomato Juice!

10:48.790 --> 10:51.010
It's not Tomato, it's Matoma.

10:51.010 --> 10:54.470
For your sake, you should end that lifestyle
of spewing random words from your mouth.

10:54.470 --> 10:56.180
What did you say?!

10:56.180 --> 10:59.720
Yes, that's enough of the usual comic stand-up.

11:00.140 --> 11:02.470
Well, it's true that we meet above often.

11:02.470 --> 11:04.850
But, it's been a while since we've met on the ground.

11:04.850 --> 11:06.770
That's why, "it's been a while".

11:06.770 --> 11:07.900
That's sophism.

11:07.900 --> 11:09.940
Correct, sophism.

11:10.320 --> 11:12.990
You really are an interesting person.

11:12.990 --> 11:14.400
My interest in you keeps growing.

11:15.030 --> 11:18.160
Shigofumi postal workers are dead people.

11:18.160 --> 11:20.950
Thus, they shouldn't age.

11:20.950 --> 11:24.080
But, you're different. You're getting older.

11:24.080 --> 11:26.370
You get bigger each time I see you.

11:27.750 --> 11:29.170
Say, Fumika...

11:29.630 --> 11:31.840
What exactly are you?

11:32.130 --> 11:34.130
Shigofumi

11:35.170 --> 11:37.180
Shigofumi

11:44.060 --> 11:46.310
Home run! Third one this season!

11:46.310 --> 11:47.020
Hey!

11:47.020 --> 11:49.980
Are you really okay, Senpai?

11:49.980 --> 11:52.980
Oh, shut up! You talk too much, Aota!

11:54.240 --> 11:56.200
Okay, one more round.

11:57.450 --> 11:59.450
Sumire Garden

12:11.880 --> 12:14.300
I'm going to deliver the curry.

12:14.300 --> 12:15.170
Please do.

12:20.930 --> 12:22.010
Are you okay?

12:22.600 --> 12:24.720
Yeah. I'm fine.

12:24.720 --> 12:26.930
Don't lie. You're acting strange today.

12:26.930 --> 12:28.310
I'm not.

12:32.690 --> 12:36.150
So, who is Tateishi Naoko?

12:39.660 --> 12:40.950
My mother.

12:41.410 --> 12:42.830
Yours?

12:42.830 --> 12:46.290
But, didn't you say that she passed away a long time ago?

12:46.950 --> 12:47.960
I made that up.

12:47.960 --> 12:50.960
Actually, she had an affair with another man and left.

12:51.420 --> 12:53.710
It happened over ten years ago.

12:54.420 --> 12:57.550
I hated and detested her.

12:58.050 --> 13:03.510
That's why, when I heard that she got
tricked by that man and got beaten up...

13:04.010 --> 13:06.140
I thought, "you got what you deserved!"

13:07.470 --> 13:08.390
Ran...

13:24.120 --> 13:25.450
Nanae.

13:33.250 --> 13:34.420
Even all the way here...

13:38.760 --> 13:41.380
Fine! I just have to accept it, right?

13:45.850 --> 13:48.220
That letter is from your mother!

13:48.220 --> 13:51.020
You're her daughter, aren't you? Read it.

13:52.100 --> 13:54.900
I'm free to choose what I do with the letter, aren't I?

13:56.110 --> 13:58.110
Yes, that's correct.

13:58.110 --> 13:59.900
How can you accept that, Fumika?

14:00.190 --> 14:02.860
This is sacrilege against the Shigofumi.

14:02.860 --> 14:04.950
People who don't pay their respects to the dead...!

14:04.950 --> 14:09.330
Kanaka, our job is to deliver Shigofumis.

14:09.870 --> 14:14.000
The recipient is free to do whatever they wish with it.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.350
Fight! Fight!

14:32.350 --> 14:33.850
Fight! Fight!

14:33.850 --> 14:35.350
Fight! Fight!

14:35.350 --> 14:36.860
Fight! Fight!

14:36.860 --> 14:38.440
Fight! Fight!

14:38.440 --> 14:39.690
Fight! Fight!

14:39.690 --> 14:41.030
Fight! Fi-

14:43.070 --> 14:44.570
Fight! Fight!

14:44.570 --> 14:45.320
Fight!

14:48.080 --> 14:50.330
Man, I'm so pathetic.

14:51.790 --> 14:54.330
We'll go to the hospital at night.

14:54.330 --> 14:58.090
I'll get the teacher to join up with us here, and take us by car.

14:58.920 --> 15:01.340
Sorry about last night.

15:01.340 --> 15:06.010
No, it's fine. If you asked, you asked. It wasn't anything good.

15:06.760 --> 15:08.470
This is the reason behind it all, right?

15:13.520 --> 15:15.940
I'm apologising for this.

15:15.940 --> 15:16.730
Did you see us?

15:17.520 --> 15:20.650
Ran, it may not be my place to tell you...

15:21.360 --> 15:22.480
but please read it.

15:22.820 --> 15:27.160
I know you plan to throw it away, but you
will become more concerned about it instead.

15:27.950 --> 15:29.780
You should know it yourself.

15:38.920 --> 15:39.960
I know you're scared.

15:40.880 --> 15:43.550
It's okay. I'm here.

15:44.760 --> 15:47.680
I'll always be by your side.

15:48.430 --> 15:51.260
So... So...

16:32.350 --> 16:34.810
Nanae, you tease.

16:54.620 --> 16:58.000
One, two, three...

16:58.290 --> 17:01.750
four, five, six...

16:58.290 --> 16:59.620
That's right...

16:59.620 --> 17:01.040
C-Captain!

17:01.540 --> 17:02.250
What is it?

17:04.630 --> 17:08.550
Fire? Is that coming from the camp house?

17:28.610 --> 17:30.360
What did you come here for?

17:30.360 --> 17:33.950
I hope you're not thinking of saving humans?

17:34.240 --> 17:35.660
Don't try.

17:35.660 --> 17:40.160
We are messengers between the living and
the dead. We can't directly involve ourselves.

17:40.660 --> 17:43.460
It's the 14th major offence set by the Gospel Department.

17:43.460 --> 17:44.880
If you violate that rule...

17:44.880 --> 17:45.920
You got it wrong.

17:45.920 --> 17:47.460
Fumika is very earnest.

17:47.460 --> 17:50.800
She's here to make sure that the
Shigofumi was safely delivered. That's all.

17:51.090 --> 17:53.140
Am I right, Fumika?

18:22.000 --> 18:23.370
I want to see...

18:31.420 --> 18:33.970
Mum...

19:02.370 --> 19:05.210
Yes. Please contact the fire department.

19:05.750 --> 19:07.710
Yes. Please do so, Teacher.

19:08.500 --> 19:10.550
Captain, what did the teacher say?

19:10.550 --> 19:12.420
Aota-san, handle the rest.

19:14.720 --> 19:15.880
Captain?

19:21.560 --> 19:22.970
Mum...

19:23.810 --> 19:25.020
No...

19:25.850 --> 19:27.230
Don't go.

19:27.900 --> 19:29.440
Mum...

19:33.740 --> 19:36.490
Mum! Where are you going?

19:37.280 --> 19:39.830
Mum, don't go!

19:39.830 --> 19:41.330
Mum!

19:41.330 --> 19:42.330
Mum!

19:42.330 --> 19:44.290
Mum!

19:46.080 --> 19:47.250
Ran?!

19:48.380 --> 19:49.540
Ran?!

19:50.880 --> 19:52.210
Ran?!

19:53.510 --> 19:56.220
Hey, what did you just do?

19:56.220 --> 19:57.800
It wasn't me.

19:57.800 --> 20:00.100
This was by someone else.

20:00.100 --> 20:00.970
Someone else?

20:02.720 --> 20:04.350
What kind rain.

20:12.150 --> 20:14.280
Forgive me, Ran.

20:16.110 --> 20:18.990
I have so much to apologise for that it'd probably be endless.

20:19.950 --> 20:21.870
But, I'm sorry.

20:22.780 --> 20:26.410
Even though you had such a bad mother, you've grown up well.

20:26.410 --> 20:28.290
You're sure a hard worker.

20:31.210 --> 20:33.500
In your first tennis game...

20:33.500 --> 20:37.670
you were positive till the very end, even though you lost.

20:37.970 --> 20:39.340
You were great.

20:39.890 --> 20:43.680
In the tournament the following year, you returned the favour.

20:44.180 --> 20:46.310
You had always hated losing.

20:47.600 --> 20:51.770
During the Inter-High semi-finals, it was the linesman's fault.

20:51.770 --> 20:54.070
That final serve was definitely in.

20:56.900 --> 20:58.650
In the team competition in Year 2...

20:58.650 --> 21:00.320
you were terrific!

21:00.740 --> 21:03.910
You got a point back for your team mates who lost.

21:05.330 --> 21:07.750
Ran, do your best!

21:08.250 --> 21:10.210
Do your best, Ran!

21:14.460 --> 21:15.460
That's so cold!

21:15.460 --> 21:16.130
That's so cold!

21:20.180 --> 21:22.590
She's really stupid.

21:22.590 --> 21:24.970
She even came to watch my practice games.

21:24.970 --> 21:27.100
She wrote about each and every one in great detail.

21:27.680 --> 21:29.600
She's really stupid.

21:30.230 --> 21:32.020
Aren't you glad you read it?

21:34.820 --> 21:35.820
Say...

21:37.320 --> 21:40.860
What kind of person was your mother?

21:47.700 --> 21:49.000
A tease.

21:51.160 --> 21:56.000
Shigofumi

21:51.160 --> 21:56.000
Episode Four

21:51.160 --> 21:56.000
Tears

23:27.010 --> 23:28.550
Things that you're not good at.

23:28.550 --> 23:29.930
Things that you love.

23:30.430 --> 23:32.430
The respective feelings of people.

23:32.720 --> 23:34.890
The person running straight at you.

23:36.270 --> 23:38.020
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:38.520 --> 23:39.230
I'm home.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Shigofumi

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Episode Five

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
I'm home
